/-!
# The binary almost-special branch

The genuine C₃ natural-action input is specified with its literal star
map and equivariant coordinates. `Setup.binary_source_lemma` proves all
seven G.2.3 conclusions for n=1: the S₃ quotient and Sylow image, I=LU,
the core product and normal series, the natural quotient with its marked
fixed spaces, and the order formula. Its action uses the original star
map and its multiplicity is shared by the tensor and order formula.

Only U≤T and Φ(U)≤V₁ from the preceding G.2.2 remain explicit. The
G.2 assembly owner discharges those inputs through CentralClosure.

The later marked 12.8.9 application is in Binary.Parabolic, keeping the
general source branch independent of its Chapter 12 consumer.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, G.2.3, printed pp.333–334.
-/
